## 10. Standardized Lexicon & Taxonomy Glossary

| Term / Taxonomy | Category | Clear & Accessible Definition |
|:---|:---|:---|
| **Martial Soul (*Wuhun*)** | Ontology | A metaphysical spiritual entity bonded to the human soul and awakened at age six, manifesting as tools, beasts, plants, or body parts. |
| **Tool Martial Soul (*Qiwuhun*)** | Taxonomy | A martial soul external to the flesh, manifesting as weapons, shields, musical instruments, food, or mechanical apparatuses. |
| **Beast Martial Soul (*Shouwuhun*)** | Taxonomy | A martial soul embodying animal or mythic beast lineage, merging directly into the user's anatomy upon possession. |
| **Body Martial Soul (*Bentai Wuhun*)** | Taxonomy | A martial soul manifesting as a part of or the entirety of the host's physical body, exhibiting superior direct combat control. |
| **Ultimate Attribute (*Jizhi*)** | Energy | The highest theoretical purity and density of an element, conferring absolute hierarchical dominance over lower-tier elements. |
| **Martial Soul Avatar (*Wuhun Zhenshen*)** | Power | The 7th Ring milestone granting full physical or spectral embodiment of the soul with massive attribute amplification. |
| **Innate Full Soul Power (*Xiantian Man Hunli*)** | Cultivation | Awakening with Rank 10 soul power at age six, representing the highest mortal cultivation ceiling at birth. |
| **Sanderson Hard Ceiling** | Narrative | Explicit limitations, costs, and failure modes ensuring power systems remain grounded, consistent, and believable. |

